  "worked_solution": "To solve the inequality $p(x)\\ge 0,$ we need to find the values of $x$ for which the curve $y=p(x)$ lies above the $x$-axis or touches this axis. \n\nBased on the graph, the solution is\n\n$$\nx\\in [\\,-3,-1]\u22c3[1,3]\u22c3[4,\\infty ).\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007649/assets/77f15f6fdfc055595bfff4d946e993c8cccd72f3fcc67e732c7d6b6abde2abec.png)",
